{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"operatic-melting-egg","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\n\n`_PROVIDER_PREFIXES` maps the `gemini` prefix to the provider name `google_genai`, but no runtime\nregistry knows that name, so any bare `gemini-*` model id resolves to a provider that cannot be\nconstructed and dies at call time.\n\nCONFIRMED INDEPENDENTLY TWICE, by two agents, on DIFFERENT bases — once against the epic stack and\nonce against plain `origin/main` — so it is not an artifact of the unlanded provider-seam work:\n\n    infer_provider('gemini-2.5-pro')                 -> 'google_genai'\n    'google_genai' in _pydantic_ai_known_providers() -> False\n    ProviderSession._builders                        -> ['anthropic', 'bedrock']\n                                                        ('openai' only when base_url is set)\n    ProviderSession.is_resolvable('google_genai')    -> False\n    ProviderSession.provider_factory('google_genai') -> LLMConfigError:\n        unknown provider 'google_genai'; registered providers: ['anthropic', 'bedrock']\n\npydantic-ai recognises `google`, `google-cloud`, `google-gla`, `google-vertex`, `vertexai` and\n`gateway/google-cloud`. It does NOT recognise `google_genai`. rebar builds only `anthropic` and\n`bedrock` (plus `openai` conditionally). So the mapped name matches nothing on either side.\n\nThe failure is at CALL time, not config time: an operator who sets a `gemini-*` model gets a\nplausible-looking config that fails only when a gate actually runs.\n\n## Location\n\nOn `origin/main` the mapping is at `src/rebar/llm/config.py:322` with `infer_provider` at `:333`;\nthe unknown-provider raise is at `src/rebar/llm/providers.py:173`. Line numbers differ on the\nprovider-seam stack — resolve them against whatever base the fix is written on.\n\n## Relationship to 7b22 — separate, and on a different path\n\n7b22 changes how a provider QUALIFIER is detected (registry membership rather than prefix shape).\nThis bug is on the INFERENCE path, which 7b22 does not touch, and it reproduces with 7b22's work\nabsent. 7b22's plan currently proposes adding `google_genai` to its `KNOWN_PROVIDER_NAMES` set to\npreserve a back-compat test — that would make an unusable name a first-class member, so this ticket\nshould be settled before that choice is locked in.\n\n## Approach\n\nDecide what `gemini` should infer to, then make the mapping and the registry agree. Options to weigh\nin the plan: map to a provider pydantic-ai actually knows (`google-gla` for the Gemini API,\n`google-vertex` for Vertex) and confirm rebar can build it; or drop the `gemini` prefix mapping so a\nbare `gemini-*` id fails at CONFIG time with an actionable message rather than at call time.\n\nWhichever is chosen, the mapping table and the buildable-provider registry must not be able to\ndisagree silently again — a test should assert every value in `_PROVIDER_PREFIXES` is resolvable.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- AC1: A bare `gemini-*` model id either resolves to a provider that `ProviderSession` can build,\n  or fails at configuration time with a message naming the supported alternatives.\n- AC2: No value in `_PROVIDER_PREFIXES` maps to a provider name absent from both\n  `_pydantic_ai_known_providers()` and `ProviderSession._builders`. A test pins this for the WHOLE\n  table, not just the gemini entry, so the next added prefix cannot reintroduce the class of defect.\n- AC3: Inference for `claude-*` and for already-qualified ids is unchanged, pinned by test.\n- AC4: make lint and make typecheck pass by exit code; the default selection is green.","id":"5267-f026-0f2b-4c02","parent_id":"061c-ecd1-8967-4a76","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"infer_provider maps gemini to google_genai, a provider neither registry knows: every bare gemini-* id is unusable"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785687853069365001,"uuid":"bb90c73b-c087-4557-a093-baa2a81a4ee9"}